hi there guys Lucy here with a less than  cheery gamespot news update for you in  the wake of the cancellation of the  world of darkness MMO CCP games have  announced that they're closing their San  Francisco office and our parting ways  with two chief execs the Icelandic  company announced the news this week in  an earning statement which was  translated by gamasutra for the six  month period that ended on the thirtieth  of June CCP games reported sales of 36  point five million dollars which is only  down marginally compared to last year's  36.7 million however the company also  reported a twenty two point eight  million dollar loss for the same time  period compared to a profit of 319,000  last year the turn and fortune was due  in part to the cancellation of the world  of darkness MMO in April which CCP games  said negatively impacted profitability  substantially due to significant  severance expenses among other things as  part of the game's cancellation 56  employees were immediately let go and in  june of this year an additional 49 jobs  were cut as part of a wider  restructuring process CFO Joe gallo and  CMO David Reed have also left the  company although CCP games  representatives have said that the split  with an amicable one going forward CCP  manager Hilmar Biograph Patterson said  the studio will focus on eve online to  boost profits the studio is also working  on a Valkyrie a dog fighting game for  the oculus rift and project Morpheus  virtual reality headsets which stars  Battlestar Galactica's Katee Sackhoff I  told you it wasn't a cheery one best of  luck to all of those affected by the  layoffs were you excited for World of  Darkness are you pumped for eval curry  let me know in the comments for the  latest gaming space faring stay tuned  here to gamespot
 

